<!--
  Brahms' Lullaby
  Wiegenlied (Lullaby), Op. 49 No. 4. Johannes Brahms (1868). Public domain.
  C major (the original is in E flat), 3/4, quarter = 80, pickup + 16 bars (36 s).
  Melody only, C4-C5, in the C4-B5 window.

  bar | right hand  | words
    0 | E4 E4       | Lul-la-
    1 | G4 E4 E4    | -by, and good
    2 | G4 E4 G4    | night, with
    3 | C5 B4 A4    | ro-ses be-
    4 | A4 G4 D4 E4 | -dight, with
    5 | F4 D4 D4 E4 | lil-ies o'er-
    6 | F4 D4 F4    | -spread is
    7 | B4 A4 G4 B4 | ba-by's wee
    8 | C5 C4 C4    | bed. Lay thee
    9 | C5 A4 F4    | down now and
   10 | G4 E4 C4    | rest, may thy
   11 | F4 G4 A4    | slum-ber be
   12 | G4 C4 C4    | blessed. Lay thee
   13 | C5 A4 F4    | down now and
   14 | G4 E4 C4    | rest, may thy
   15 | F4 E4 D4    | slum-ber be
   16 | C4          | blessed.
-->
